---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { absoluteUrl, href } from "../lib/paths";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "AboutPage",
  name: "About Move-Out Desk",
  url: absoluteUrl("/about"),
  description:
    "Independence and affiliate disclosure for Move-Out Desk, a Texas A&M storage comparison.",
  isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", name: "Move-Out Desk", url: absoluteUrl("/") },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About this comparison and the affiliate disclosure"
  description="Move-Out Desk is independent of Texas A&M and of the storage companies it lists. No affiliate programs are joined. Sponsored links, when they exist, will be marked."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p class="crumbs"><a href={href("/")}>Home</a> / About</p>
  <p class="eyebrow">Disclosure</p>
  <h1>Independent on purpose, and not paid yet.</h1>
  <div class="prose stack">
    <p>
      Move-Out Desk compares college move-out and summer storage. The first campus is Texas A&M in
      College Station. The pages are a template: a school file, a city file, and one file per
      provider. Later directories can reuse that shape. This version is only storage.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are not Texas A&M University, not the residence halls, and not affiliated with Collegeboxes,
      Dorm Room Movers, U-Haul, CubeSmart, SpareBox, Anytime Storage, or Lock N Roll. Collegeboxes
      prints its own line that it has no active partnership with Texas A&M University, College
      Station. That matches how you should read every link here. A company page is a source, not an
      endorsement.
    </p>
    <h2>What we will publish</h2>
    <p>
      A price, a date, a fee, or an hour goes on the site when we can open a public page that states
      it. The row keeps that URL and a last-verified date. If the pages disagree, we show both and
      mark the row as a conflict. If we cannot find the number, the cell says not yet verified.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not publish star ratings, review scores, or quotes from named students. Forum threads
      are used only to see which questions people ask and which facility names come up.
    </p>
    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      None of the outbound links are affiliate links. The programs have not been joined, and nothing
      on this site is written to earn a commission. Each provider file has an <code>affiliateUrl</code>
      field, and today every one of those fields is null.
    </p>
    <p>
      When a program is joined later, that field gets the tracking URL. The template will point the
      outbound link at it and set <code>rel="sponsored nofollow"</code>. The visible link will also
      carry a Sponsored marker. A link with an empty affiliate field stays a normal link to the
      company's own page. Editorial pages will keep saying when a figure was checked, whether or not
      a link pays.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Storage prices move. A row that was right on November 18, 2026 can be wrong next week. There
      is no contact form on this version. The reliable check is the source link on the row. If you
      are about to pay, use the company's page, not our table, as the invoice.
    </p>
    <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
    <ul class="clean">
      <li>No accounts, no booking, and no payment.</li>
      <li>No analytics, advertising pixels, or other trackers.</li>
      <li>No invented "most students choose" claims.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
